WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.380
He wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.430
Saving people,hunting
things. The family business.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.130
Today's your lucky day,kid.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.030
You watch out for sammy,okay?
Yeah,dad. You know I will.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.040
Dad.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.560
Time of death -10:41 A.M.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.990
I miss him,man,and I'm not
all right. Neither are you.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.970
I'm dealing with dad's death!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.650
Dad's dead,and it hurts
so bad, you can't take it.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.370
I'm okay! I swear,the next
person who asks if I'm okay,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.280
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.210
Okay,we got booze...

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.420
We got chocolate...

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.020
And...wait for it.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.650
Tortured emo rock.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.840
Guaranteed cure for any broken heart.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.080
You didn't have to do all this.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.700
I'm fine.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.470
Yeah,I can see that.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.610
Thanks,neal.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.890
You're a good friend.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.300
It's probably him.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.410
I'll take care of it.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:19.700
Where is she?

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.810
Chill out and think about this,okay?

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.330
I need to talk to her. Some other time.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.570
You get out of my face now.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.280
Angela?

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:56.960
Leave...me...alone.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.730
Angela,I'm sorry.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.930
You're sorry?

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.190
You're sorry? Oh,that's great.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.540
Angela,listen to me.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.140
I don't want to listen to you!

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.890
I'm done listening! Listen to me.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.880
How could you do this? I loved you.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.290
Angela?

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.030
Angela!

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.660
Come on,sam. I'm begging
you. This is stupid.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.700
Why?

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.870
Going to visit mom's grave?

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:58.130
She doesn't even have a grave. There
was no body left after the fire.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.290
She has a headstone.

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.500
Put up by our uncle, a
man that we've never met.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.980
You want to pay your respects to a
slab of granite put up by a stranger.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.460
That's not the point. Then enlighten me.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.450
It's not about a body or a casket.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.250
It's about her memory, okay?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.850
And after
dad,it just --

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.580
It just feels like
the right thing to do.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.030
It's irrational is what it is.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.650
Look,man, no one asked you to come.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.340
Why don't we swing by
the roadhouse instead?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.190
We haven't heard anything on the demon lately.
We should be hunting that son of a bitch down.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.780
That's a good idea. You should.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.050
Just drop me off,I'll hitch a ride,
and I'll meet you there tomorrow.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.940
Right.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:38.360
Stuck with those people, making
awkward small talk until you show up.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.160
No,thanks.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.400
I think,uh...

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.190
I think dad would have
wanted you to have these.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.650
I love you,mom.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.100
Thank you.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.500
Angela mason.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.600
She was a student at the local
college. Her funeral was three days ago.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:04.280
And?

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:05.660
And?

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.210
You saw her grave -- Everything
dead around it in a perfect circle.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.540
You don't think that's a little weird?

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.730
Maybe the grounds keeper went a
little agro with the pesticide.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:16.730
No,I asked him. No pesticide,no
chemicals. Nobody can explain it.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.490
Okay, so,what are you thinking?

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:22.050
I don't know. Unholy ground,maybe.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.890
What?

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:27.830
If something evil happened,it
could easily poison the ground.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.230
Remember the farm
outside of cedar rapids?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:30.930
Yeah.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:34.020
It could be the sign
of a demonic presence

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.820
Or the angela girl's spirit,
if it's powerful enough.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.760
Well,don't get too excited.
You might pull something.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.890
It's just stumbling onto a hunt...

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.750
Here of all places? So?

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.270
So,are you sure this is about
a hunt,not something else?

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.740
What else would it be about?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:56.850
Just forget it.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.900
Believe what you want,sam,

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:02.020
But I let you drag my ass out here.
The least we can do is check this out.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.410
Yeah,fine.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:09.420
The girl's dad works in town.
He's a professor at the school.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.810
Dr. Mason? Yes.

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.350
I'm sam. This is dean.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:31.400
We were friends of angela'S.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:35.020
We -We wanted to offer our condolences.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.420
Please come in.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.520
She was beautiful.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.600
Yes,she was.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.420
This is an unusual book.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:00.690
It's ancient greek. I teach a course.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:11.100
So,a car accident.
That's -That's horrible.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.960
Angie was only a mile
away from home when...

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:20.980
It's got to be hard...
losing someone like that.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.300
Sometimes it's like
they're still around,

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:29.510
Almost like you can still
sense their presence.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.280
You ever feel anything like that?

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.110
I do,as a matter of fact.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.970
That's perfectly normal, dr. Mason,

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:42.290
Especially with what
you're going through.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.140
You know, I still phone her.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:50.430
And the phone's ringing
before I remember that,uh...

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.800
Family's everything, you know?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.010
Angie was the most
important thing in my life.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:03.900
And now I'm just lost without her.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.020
I'm very sorry.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:16.070
There's something going on.
We just haven't found it yet.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:20.560
Dean,so far you got a patch
of dead grass and nothing.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.800
Well,something turned that
grave into unholy ground.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:25.350
There's no reason for
it to be unholy ground.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.660
Angela mason was a nice
girl who died in a car crash.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.100
That's not exactly
vengeful-Spirit material.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.660
You heard her father.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.450
Maybe daddy doesn't know  everything
there is to know about his little angel,

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:38.750
You know what? We never should
have bothered that poor man.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.490
We shouldn't even be here anymore.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:44.560
So,what,sam?We just bail without
even figuring out what's going on?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.720
I think I know what's going on here.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.400
It's the only reason I went
along with you this far.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.610
What are you talking about?
This is about mom's grave.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.710
Got nothing to do with it.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.830
You wouldn't step
within 100 yards of it.

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:03.410
Look,maybe you're imagining
a hunt where there isn't one

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:07.250
So you don't have to
think about mom or dad.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.160
You want to take another swing? Go ahead

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.650
If it will make you feel better.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.140
I don't need this crap.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:31.040
Dean,where are you going?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.710
I'm gonna go get a drink...

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.630
Alone.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.510
Who the hell are you?!
Wait,wait,wait,wait.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.000
Hold on!

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.540
I'm calling 911!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.090
'M angela's cousin. What?

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:39.380
Yeah,her dad sent me
over to pick up her stuff.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:42.710
My name's alan
-- Alan stanwick.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.830
Her dad didn't say that you were coming.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.760
Well,I mean...

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:55.840
How else would I have
the key to your place?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:11.490
So,I'm sure you got a view of angela
that none of the family got to see.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.560
Tell me,what was she like?

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.160
What was she really like?

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.150
She was great...

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.610
Just...great.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.190
I mean,she was so...

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:26.940
Great.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:29.390
Yeah.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.230
Yeah.

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:38.540
You two must have been really close,huh?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.020
We were.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.580
But it's not just her, it's matt.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.560
Who?

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.160
Angela's boyfriend.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.260
Right -Matt.

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.110
Uh,what about him?

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:54.640
He killed himself last night.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.900
He cut his own throat. Who does that?

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:01.190
That'S...terrible.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:05.350
He was taking angela's death
pretty hard,and I guess...

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.240
I mean,he'd been messed
up about it for days.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.480
Messed up how?

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.370
He kept saying that
he saw her everywhere.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.290
Well,I'm -- I'm
sure that's normal.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.250
I mean,with everything
he was going through.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.960
He said that he saw her...

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.120
As in an acid trip or something.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.580
Were angela and matt a happy couple?

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.340
I mean,was there any reason that
angela would be angry with him?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.120
What?

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:34.880
No,of course not. Why do you ask?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.960
Just asking.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.680
Where did matt live?

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.610
Next on cinemax,

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.710
"Casa erotica iv,"

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.730
A tale of two latin beauties,

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.910
Hey.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.280
What?

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.160
Awkward.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.950
Where the hell were you? Just
working my imaginary case.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.050
Yeah? And?

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:06.840
Oh,well,you were right.
I didn't find much.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.770
Yeah. Except angela's
boyfriend died last night --

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.380
Slit his own throat,
but,you know,that's normal.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:13.720
Uh,let's see. What else?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.550
Oh,he was seeing angela
everywhere before he died.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:20.880
But,you know,I'm sure  that's just
me transferring my own feelings.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.430
Okay,I get it.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.260
I'm sorry. Maybe there is
something going on here.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:25.910
Maybe?

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:29.910
Sam,I know how to do my job
despite what you might think.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.790
We should check out the guy's apartment.

00:15:34.210 --> 00:15:36.350
I just came from there...

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:39.280
A pile of dead plants
just like the cemetery.

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:41.040
Hell,a dead goldfish,too.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.730
So,unholy ground? Maybe.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:47.710
I'm still not getting that powerful
angry-Spirit vibe from angela.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.280
I've been reading this, though.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.550
You stole the girl's diary? Yeah,sam.

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.900
And if anything, the
girl's a little too nice.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.320
So,what do you want to do?

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.110
Keep digging, talk to
more of her friends.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.640
You get any names? You kidding me?

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:11.020
I have her bestest friend
in the whole wide world.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:15.620
I didn't realize the college
employed grief counselors.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:16.810
Oh,yeah.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.520
Yeah,you talk,we listen

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.630
And maybe throw in a little therapeutic
collage whatever helps jump-Start the healing.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:25.910
Well,I think I'm okay. Thanks.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.850
Well,you heard what happened
to matt harrison,right?

00:16:28.850 --> 00:16:30.230
Yeah,I did.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.980
We just wanted to make
sure you were okay.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:36.380
Grief can make people do crazy things.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:41.720
Look,I'm sorry about
what happened to him.I am.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.690
But if matt killed himself,
it wasn't 'cause of grief.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.390
No? Then why?

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.420
It was guilt.

00:16:48.420 --> 00:16:50.770
Angie's death was matt's
fault, and he knew it.

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:52.620
How was matt responsible?

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.040
She really loved that guy,

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:58.620
But the night of the accident, she
walked in on him with another girl.

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:03.900
She was really torn up.
That's why she crashed.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.370
Um,look, I got to get ready for work,

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:12.790
So thanks for the concern,
but,seriously,I'll be okay.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.680
Well,my vengeful-Spirit theory is
starting to make a little more sense.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.280
I mean,hell hath no fury.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:27.350
So,if angela got her revenge
on matt,you think it's over?

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.790
Well, there's one way to be sure.

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.740
Yeah? What's that?

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:36.750
Burn the bones.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.810
Burn the bones?

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:42.890
Are you high? Angela died last week.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.250
So?

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.840
So there's not gonna be bones. There's
gonna be a ripe,rotting body in the coffin.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:51.810
Since when are you
afraid to get dirty,huh?

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:19.490
Ladies first.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:24.440
Hold that.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.670
I missed you.

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.150
They buried the body four days ago.

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:29.620
I don't get it.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.210
Look.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:37.090
What is that? I'm not sure.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.160
I've seen these kinds of symbols before.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:46.040
Dean,take it easy,okay?

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:54.820
You're angie's friends.

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:57.350
Dr. Mason --
We need to talk.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.890
Well,come in.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:02.370
Thanks.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.620
You teach ancient greek.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.640
Tell me...

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.100
What are these?

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:15.630
I don't understand.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:18.370
You said this had
something to do with angela.

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:21.500
It does. Please,just humor me.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:26.470
They're part of an ancient
greek divination ritual.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:28.990
Used for necromancy,right. That's right.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:30.110
See, before we came over here,

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:33.290
We stopped by the library and
did a little homework ourselves.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:37.430
Apparently, they use rituals like this
one for communicating with the dead,

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:41.320
Even bringing corpses back to
life -Full-On zombie action.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.230
Yeah.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:46.490
I mean, according to the legends.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.450
Now,what's this all about?

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.510
I think you know. Dean.

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:53.540
Look,I get it.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.740
There are people that I would
give anything to see again,

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:57.910
But what gives you the right?

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.160
Dean. What are you talking about?

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.720
What's dead should stay dead! What?

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:03.180
Stop it! What you brought
back isn't your daughter!

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.700
These things are
vicious, they're violent!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.850
They're so nasty, they
rot the ground around them.

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:10.540
I mean,come on! Haven't
you seen "pet sematary"?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.150
You're insane.

00:21:13.550 --> 00:21:16.380
Where is she? Get out of my house.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:18.650
I know you're hiding her
somewhere. Where is she?!

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:20.960
Dean,stop! That's
enough. Dean,look --

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:25.180
Beautiful,living plants. We're leaving.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:27.350
I'm calling the police. Sir,we're sorry.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:30.010
We won't bother you again.

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:35.040
What the hell's the
matter with you? Back off.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:37.380
That man is innocent.
He didn't deserve that.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.640
So she's not here. Maybe he's
keeping her somewhere else.

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.800
Stop it! That's enough,okay? Enough!

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.150
Sam,I know what I'm doing.
No,you don'T...at all.

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:47.670
I don't scare easy,but you're
scaring the crap out of me.

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.140
Don't be overdramatic, sam.

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.090
You're lucky this turned
out to be a real case,

00:21:51.090 --> 00:21:54.180
'Cause if it wasn't,you would've
found something else to kill.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:56.070
You're on edge, you're erratic,

00:21:56.070 --> 00:21:58.880
Except for when you're hunting,'cause
then you're downright scary.

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.870
You're tailspinning,man,

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:04.380
And you refuse to talk about it,
and you won't let me help you.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.870
I can take care of myself, thanks.

00:22:05.870 --> 00:22:07.750
No,you can't!

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:11.020
And you're the only one who
thinks you should have to.

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:13.420
You don't have to handle
this on your own. No one can.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:17.170
If you bring up dad's death one more
time -- Dean,it's killing you. Please.

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:22.360
We've already lost dad.

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.200
We lost mom.

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:27.230
I've lost jessica.

00:22:27.230 --> 00:22:30.190
And now I'm gonna lose you,too?

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.580
We better get out of
here before the cops come.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.190
I hear you,okay?

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.920
I'm being an ass, and I'm sorry.

00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:44.660
But we got a freakin' zombie running
around. We need to figure out how to kill it.

00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:49.400
Right?

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:51.820
Our lives are weird,man.

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:54.100
You're telling me.

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:57.650
Come on.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:01.720
Honey, is something bothering you?

00:23:03.290 --> 00:23:05.140
It's about matt.

00:23:05.140 --> 00:23:06.990
Haven't we already talked about that?

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.190
I
know,but,uh --

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:11.750
Haven't we wasted enough
time on him already?

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.460
Come sit down.

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:26.000
You always said that
he didn't deserve me.

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:29.250
You were right. Angela...

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:35.430
You didn't get out and go see matt or...

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.610
I've been here the whole time.

00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:43.870
Neal...you really think I
could do something like that?

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:46.580
No,I... I don't know.

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.130
I can't help it. You just -You seem...

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:52.000
Different?

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:55.990
You're right. I am.

00:23:58.650 --> 00:24:01.380
I've realized...

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:04.940
You're the only one who
ever really loved me.

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:11.410
You proved that. You brought me back.

00:24:11.410 --> 00:24:13.910
I'm with you now.

00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:18.050
Isn't that what you always wanted?

00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:23.340
We can't just waste
her with a head shot?

00:24:23.340 --> 00:24:26.160
Dude,you've been wahing
way too many romero flicks.

00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:28.260
You're telling me there's
no lore on how to smoke them?

00:24:28.260 --> 00:24:30.580
No,I'm telling you there's too much.

00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:32.660
There's 100 different
legends on the walking dead,

00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:34.560
But they all have different
methods for killing them.

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:38.980
Some say setting them on
fire. One said -Where is it?

00:24:38.980 --> 00:24:41.340
Right here -Feeding
their hearts to wild dogs.

00:24:41.340 --> 00:24:43.170
That's my personal favorite.

00:24:43.170 --> 00:24:44.830
But who knows what's
real and what's myth?

00:24:44.830 --> 00:24:46.410
Is there anything they have in common?

00:24:46.410 --> 00:24:48.640
No,but a few said silver might work.

00:24:48.640 --> 00:24:50.130
Silver's a start.

00:24:50.130 --> 00:24:51.860
But now how are we going to find angela?

00:24:51.860 --> 00:24:53.540
We got to figure out
who brought her back.

00:24:53.540 --> 00:24:55.160
Any ideas?

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:58.210
I think if it's not her dad,
it might be that guy,neal.

00:24:58.210 --> 00:24:59.610
Neal? Yep.

00:24:59.610 --> 00:25:02.380
How'd you come up with that?
Well,you got your journal,I got mine.

00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:05.190
"Neal's a real shoulder to cry on.

00:25:05.190 --> 00:25:08.980
He so understands what I'm
going through with matt."

00:25:08.980 --> 00:25:13.070
There's more here where that came from. It's
got unrequited duckie love written all over it.

00:25:13.070 --> 00:25:15.550
But that doesn't mean he
brought her back from the dead.

00:25:15.550 --> 00:25:18.080
Hmm,did I mention that
he's professor mason's T.A.?

00:25:18.080 --> 00:25:21.010
Has access to all the same books.

00:25:26.450 --> 00:25:28.250
Hello?

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:33.750
Neal!

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:37.150
It's your grief counselors.
We've come to hug.

00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:42.180
Silver bullets?

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:45.380
Yeah,enough to make her
rattle like a change purse.

00:26:11.630 --> 00:26:14.030
Unless it's where he keeps his porn.

00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:44.440
It sure looks like a zombie pen to me.

00:26:44.440 --> 00:26:45.850
Yeah.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.390
An empty one.

00:26:49.830 --> 00:26:52.750
You think angela's gone after somebody?

00:27:02.180 --> 00:27:04.240
No,I think she went
out to rent "beaches."

00:27:04.240 --> 00:27:07.310
Look,smartass. She might kill someone.

00:27:07.310 --> 00:27:09.550
We got to find her,dean.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:12.170
Yeah.

00:27:12.730 --> 00:27:15.710
All right,she clipped matt
because he was cheating,right?

00:27:15.710 --> 00:27:16.710
Yeah.

00:27:16.710 --> 00:27:21.480
Well,takes two to,you
know, have hard-Core sex.

00:27:22.360 --> 00:27:23.420
I don't know. It just seemed

00:27:23.420 --> 00:27:25.950
That angela's roommate was...

00:27:25.950 --> 00:27:29.090
Broken up over matt's death.

00:27:29.530 --> 00:27:33.850
I mean, like really broken up.

00:27:51.830 --> 00:27:54.000
Hello?

00:28:01.730 --> 00:28:03.820
Hi,lindsay. I'm home.

00:28:13.010 --> 00:28:15.000
You know what you did.

00:28:17.820 --> 00:28:18.970
I'm sorry!

00:28:18.970 --> 00:28:20.560
I am so sorry!

00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:22.380
Not sorry enough!

00:28:44.950 --> 00:28:46.120
God.

00:28:47.800 --> 00:28:49.490
God.

00:28:49.490 --> 00:28:50.960
Oh,my god.

00:28:50.960 --> 00:28:52.220
Oh,my god.

00:29:22.680 --> 00:29:24.220
I got you. I got you.

00:29:27.390 --> 00:29:29.460
Damn, that dead chick can run.

00:29:29.460 --> 00:29:31.700
What now?

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:34.620
I say we go have a
little chat with neal.

00:29:38.320 --> 00:29:41.330
So,the silver bullets,
they did something,right?

00:29:41.330 --> 00:29:44.810
Yeah,something,but not
enough. What else you got?

00:29:45.910 --> 00:29:47.380
Um,okay,besides silver,

00:29:47.380 --> 00:29:50.850
We have "nailing the undead
back into their grave beds."

00:29:50.850 --> 00:29:55.210
It's mentioned a few times. It's probably
where the whole vampire-Staking lore came from.

00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:57.410
Their grave beds? You serious?

00:29:57.410 --> 00:29:58.440
Yeah.

00:29:58.440 --> 00:30:01.650
How the hell are we gonna get
angela back to the cemetery?

00:30:13.140 --> 00:30:15.120
What are you guys doing here?

00:30:16.750 --> 00:30:19.890
You know,I've heard of some people doing
some pretty desperate things to get laid,

00:30:19.890 --> 00:30:21.610
But you

00:30:21.610 --> 00:30:23.790
You take the cake.

00:30:23.790 --> 00:30:25.380
Okay,who are you guys?

00:30:25.380 --> 00:30:27.730
You might want to ask
angela that question.

00:30:27.730 --> 00:30:29.870
What? We know what you did.

00:30:30.980 --> 00:30:33.980
The ritual...everything.

00:30:35.420 --> 00:30:36.840
You're crazy.

00:30:36.840 --> 00:30:40.170
Your girlfriend's past her
expiration date, and we're crazy?

00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:43.300
When someone's gone,
they should stay gone.

00:30:43.300 --> 00:30:46.210
You don't mess with that kind of stuff.

00:30:46.210 --> 00:30:48.460
Angela killed matt.

00:30:48.460 --> 00:30:51.400
She tried to kill lindsay.

00:30:51.400 --> 00:30:54.680
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:30:56.810 --> 00:30:58.740
Hey,no more crap,neal!

00:30:58.740 --> 00:31:01.210
This blood is on your hands.

00:31:01.210 --> 00:31:05.060
Now,me and him can make this right,
but you got to tell us where she is.

00:31:05.950 --> 00:31:07.730
Tell us!

00:31:09.880 --> 00:31:11.850
My house.

00:31:11.850 --> 00:31:13.850
She's at my house.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:26.330
You sure about that?

00:31:36.010 --> 00:31:38.260
Listen. It doesn't really
matter where she is.

00:31:39.460 --> 00:31:41.990
There's only one way to stop her.

00:31:41.990 --> 00:31:46.540
We've got to perform another ritual over
her grave  to reverse the one that you did.

00:31:47.250 --> 00:31:50.490
We're going to need some black
roots, some scar weed,some candles.

00:31:50.490 --> 00:31:52.490
It's very complicated, but
it will get the job done.

00:31:52.490 --> 00:31:54.980
She'll be dead again in a couple hours.

00:31:54.980 --> 00:31:57.210
I think you should come with us.

00:32:00.600 --> 00:32:04.270
I'm serious,neal.
Leave with us right now.

00:32:04.270 --> 00:32:05.960
No.

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:08.640
No.

00:32:13.350 --> 00:32:15.550
Listen to me.

00:32:15.550 --> 00:32:17.900
Get out of here as soon as you can.

00:32:18.960 --> 00:32:22.890
But most of all,be cool.
No sudden movements.

00:32:22.890 --> 00:32:25.860
Don't make her mad.

00:32:28.760 --> 00:32:30.270
Let's go.

00:32:46.940 --> 00:32:48.740
You said you'd stay in the house.

00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:52.100
I'm sorry. I just needed to see you.

00:32:52.380 --> 00:32:54.870
Neal,please.

00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:59.920
You have to help me.

00:33:02.620 --> 00:33:04.240
Oh,god.

00:33:04.240 --> 00:33:07.630
Come with me to the cemetery.
Neal,they're trying to kill me.

00:33:07.630 --> 00:33:09.160
We have to stop them.

00:33:09.160 --> 00:33:11.320
You mean kill them?

00:33:12.620 --> 00:33:14.610
It's
true --

00:33:14.610 --> 00:33:17.630
Matt and lindsay. They hurt me.

00:33:18.320 --> 00:33:21.420
If you love me,you'll make
sure nobody hurts me again.

00:33:21.420 --> 00:33:24.830
Take me to the cemetery,
then all this will be over.

00:33:24.830 --> 00:33:28.000
We can start new lives together.

00:33:30.090 --> 00:33:32.070
Okay.

00:33:33.330 --> 00:33:35.970
God help me,but okay.

00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:39.100
I'll go get the car.

00:33:39.100 --> 00:33:40.530
Just...

00:33:40.530 --> 00:33:42.700
Just wait here.

00:34:05.990 --> 00:34:07.980
Neal,you look nervous.

00:34:08.550 --> 00:34:10.650
No,I'm fine.

00:34:11.940 --> 00:34:14.950
Were you... going to leave me?

00:34:15.380 --> 00:34:16.940
No,of course not.

00:34:16.940 --> 00:34:19.280
You were,weren't you?!

00:34:19.280 --> 00:34:22.650
How could you?! Neal,I loved you!

00:34:22.650 --> 00:34:23.880
Angela
--

00:34:36.620 --> 00:34:39.190
You really think this is gonna work?

00:34:39.190 --> 00:34:41.770
No,not really.

00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:46.590
But it was the only thing
I could come up with.

00:35:41.850 --> 00:35:44.840
Wait. It's not what you think.

00:35:44.840 --> 00:35:48.110
I didn't ask to be brought
back, but it's still me.

00:35:48.110 --> 00:35:51.140
I'm still a person. Please.

00:36:27.090 --> 00:36:29.140
Please don't!

00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:48.470
What's dead should stay dead.

00:36:56.810 --> 00:36:58.180
Rest in peace.

00:36:58.180 --> 00:37:00.340
Yeah, for good this time,okay?

00:37:06.790 --> 00:37:08.460
You know,

00:37:08.870 --> 00:37:10.630
The whole fake-Ritual thing,

00:37:10.630 --> 00:37:14.500
Luring angela into the
cemetery -Pretty sharp.

00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:16.430
Thanks.

00:37:16.430 --> 00:37:19.010
But did we have to use me as bait?

00:37:19.010 --> 00:37:22.870
I figured you were more her type,you
know? She had pretty crappy taste in guys.

00:37:23.280 --> 00:37:25.450
I think she broke my hand.

00:37:25.950 --> 00:37:29.270
You're just too fragile.
We'll get it looked at later.

00:37:34.660 --> 00:37:36.870
You want to stay for a while?

00:37:41.580 --> 00:37:43.670
No.

00:38:51.100 --> 00:38:53.160
Dean,what is it?

00:38:57.210 --> 00:38:58.680
I'm sorry.

00:39:00.200 --> 00:39:02.160
For what?

00:39:03.890 --> 00:39:06.520
The way I've been acting.

00:39:24.350 --> 00:39:26.590
And for dad.

00:39:29.030 --> 00:39:32.180
Well, he was your dad,too.

00:39:32.970 --> 00:39:34.770
It's my fault that he's gone.

00:39:34.770 --> 00:39:36.650
What are you talking about?

00:39:36.650 --> 00:39:39.600
I know you've been
thinking it. So have I.

00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:42.960
Doesn't take a genius to figure it out.

00:39:44.340 --> 00:39:48.630
Back at the hospital,
I had a full recovery.

00:39:48.630 --> 00:39:51.410
It was a miracle.

00:39:51.410 --> 00:39:54.170
And five minutes later, dad's
dead,and the colt's gone.

00:39:54.170 --> 00:39:57.820
You can't tell me there's
not a connection there.

00:39:59.650 --> 00:40:02.690
I don't know how the demon was involved.

00:40:03.180 --> 00:40:06.680
I don't know how the whole
thing went down exactly...

00:40:07.230 --> 00:40:10.790
But dad's dead because of me.

00:40:10.790 --> 00:40:12.410
And that much I do know.

00:40:12.410 --> 00:40:14.810
We don't know that, not for sure.

00:40:14.810 --> 00:40:17.800
Sam...

00:40:19.060 --> 00:40:23.080
You and dad...

00:40:24.320 --> 00:40:27.300
You're the most important
people in my life.

00:40:27.730 --> 00:40:31.370
And now...

00:40:31.770 --> 00:40:35.340
I never should have come
back, sam. It wasn't natural.

00:40:36.830 --> 00:40:39.680
And now look what's come of it.

00:40:41.990 --> 00:40:44.250
I was dead.

00:40:45.390 --> 00:40:48.870
And I should have stayed dead.

00:40:54.490 --> 00:40:57.570
You wanted to know how I was feeling.

00:40:59.060 --> 00:41:01.830
Well,that's it.

00:41:04.300 --> 00:41:06.330
So tell me.

00:41:11.030 --> 00:41:14.620
What could you possibly
say to make that all right?



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
